  "notes": "UK garage two-step, G minor, 126 BPM, a heavy shuffle (swing 32). An organ stabbing rootless ninth shells (b3, b7, 9) on a skipping 2-step rhythm, its rotary speaker sped up by MOTION, a detuned reese bass that follows the kick, the player's FM bell on the Smart Keys with triplet echoes, and the 909 kit: a broken two-step kick, snare on 2 and 4, shuffled hats, ghost rims and a shaker. Scenes: A STATIC is hats and organ over a held Gm7; B PULL turns i7 VII iv7 in two bars; C CHARGE lifts iv7 VII IIImaj7 with claps and open hats; D DRIFT floats on IIImaj7 iv7. ENERGY: organ alone, then kick, rims and bass, then the full shuffle, then sixteenths, fills and ratchets. All material is original.",
